{"id":"cb6550ea79a67b751469b3f749ebd5e807357dab","axis":"silent","repo":"python-telegram-bot/python-telegram-bot","sha":"cb6550ea79a67b751469b3f749ebd5e807357dab","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/CONTRIBUTING.rst","lines":["@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ Setting things up"," "," 4. Install the package in development mode as well as optional dependencies and development dependencies.","    Note that the `--group` argument requires `pip` 25.1 or later.","+   The ``all`` group includes the documentation tools and requires Python 3.13 or later.","    ","    Alternatively, you can use your preferred package manager (such as uv, hatch, poetry, etc.) instead of pip."," ","@@ -167,7 +168,7 @@ Feel free to copy (parts of) the checklist to the PR description to remind you o"," ","     - [ ] Added `.. versionadded:: NEXT.VERSION`, ``.. versionchanged:: NEXT.VERSION``, ``.. deprecated:: NEXT.VERSION`` or ``.. versionremoved:: NEXT.VERSION` to the docstrings for user facing changes (for methods/class descriptions, arguments and attributes)","     - [ ] Created new or adapted existing unit tests","-    - [ ] Documented code changes according to the [CSI standard](https://standards.mousepawmedia.com/en/stable/csi.html)","+    - [ ] Documented code changes according to the [CSI standard](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mousepawmedia/standards/devel/source/csi.rst)","     - [ ] Added myself alphabetically to `AUTHORS.rst` (optional)","     - [ ] Added new classes & modules to the docs and all suitable ``__all__`` s","     - [ ] Checked the [Stability Policy](https://docs.python-telegram-bot.org/stability_policy.html) in case of deprecations or changes to documented behavior","@@ -216,7 +217,7 @@ doc strings don't have a separate documentation site they generate, instead, the"," "," User facing documentation"," -------------------------","-We use `sphinx`_ to generate static HTML docs. To build them, first make sure you're running Python 3.12 or above and have the required dependencies installed as explained above.","+We use `sphinx`_ to generate static HTML docs. To build them, first make sure you're running Python 3.13 or above and have the required dependencies installed as explained above."," Then, run the following from the PTB root directory:"," "," .. code-block:: bash","@@ -291,7 +292,7 @@ to add new required arguments. It's also more explicit and easier to read."," .. _`Ruff`: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/"," .. _`RTD`: https://docs.python-telegram-bot.org/"," .. _`RTD build`: https://docs.python-telegram-bot.org/en/doc-fixes","-.. _`CSI`: https://standards.mousepawmedia.com/en/stable/csi.html","+.. _`CSI`: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mousepawmedia/standards/devel/source/csi.rst"," .. _`section`: #documenting"," .. _`testing page`: https://github.com/python-telegram-bot/python-telegram-bot/blob/master/tests/README.rst"," .. _`below`: #check-list-for-prs"],"additions":4,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":".github/workflows/docs-admonitions.yml","lines":["@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ jobs:","       actions: write","     strategy:","       matrix:","-        python-version: ['3.12']","+        python-version: ['3.13']","         os: [ubuntu-latest]","       fail-fast: False","     steps:"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":".github/workflows/docs-linkcheck.yml","lines":["@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ jobs:","     runs-on: ${{matrix.os}}","     strategy:","       matrix:","-        python-version: ['3.12']","+        python-version: ['3.13']","         os: [ubuntu-latest]","       fail-fast: False","     steps:"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":".pre-commit-config.yaml","lines":["@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@"," repos:"," -   repo: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff-pre-commit","-    rev: 'v0.16.8'","+    rev: 'v0.17.6'","     hooks:","     # Run the linter:","     -   id: ruff-check","@@ -18,15 +18,15 @@ repos:","         files: ^(?!(tests|docs)).*\\.py$","         language: python","         additional_dependencies:","-          - httpx~=0.27","-          - tornado~=6.4","+          - httpx>=0.27,<0.29","+          - tornado~=6.5","           - APScheduler>=3.10.4,<3.12.0","           - cachetools>=8.0.0,<8.1.0","-          - aiolimiter~=1.3,<1.4","+          - aiolimiter>=1.3,<1.4","           - . # this basically does `pip install -e .`","         priority: 10"," -   repo: https://github.com/pre-commit/mirrors-mypy","-    rev: v1.20.2","+    rev: v2.4.1","     hooks:","     -   id: mypy","         name: mypy-ptb","@@ -36,11 +36,11 @@ repos:","           - types-pytz","           - types-cryptography","           - types-cachetools","-          - httpx~=0.27","-          - tornado~=6.4","+          - httpx>=0.27,<0.29","+          - tornado~=6.5","           - APScheduler>=3.10.4,<3.12.0","           - cachetools>=8.0.0,<8.1.0","-          - aiolimiter~=1.3,<1.4","+          - aiolimiter>=1.3,<1.4","           - . # this basically does `pip install -e .`","         priority: 10","     - id: mypy","@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@ repos:","         - --no-strict-optional","         - --follow-imports=silent","       additional_dependencies:","-        - tornado~=6.4","+        - tornado~=6.5","         - APScheduler>=3.10.4,<3.12.0","         - cachetools>=8.0.0,<8.1.0","         - . # this basically does `pip install -e .`"],"additions":9,"deletions":9,"truncated":false},{"path":"README.rst","lines":["@@ -153,9 +153,9 @@ PTB can be installed with optional dependencies:"," * ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[passport]\"`` installs the `cryptography>=39.0.1 <https://cryptography.io/en/stable>`_ library. Use this, if you want to use Telegram Passport related functionality."," * ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[socks]\"`` installs `httpx[socks] <https://www.python-httpx.org/#dependencies>`_. Use this, if you want to work behind a Socks5 server."," * ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[http2]\"`` installs `httpx[http2] <https://www.python-httpx.org/#dependencies>`_. Use this, if you want to use HTTP/2.","-* ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[rate-limiter]\"`` installs `aiolimiter~=1.1,<1.3 <https://aiolimiter.readthedocs.io/en/stable/>`_. Use this, if you want to use ``telegram.ext.AIORateLimiter``.","-* ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[webhooks]\"`` installs the `tornado~=6.4 <https://www.tornadoweb.org/en/stable/>`_ library. Use this, if you want to use ``telegram.ext.Updater.start_webhook``/``telegram.ext.Application.run_webhook``.","-* ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[callback-data]\"`` installs the `cachetools>=5.3.3,<6.3.0 <https://cachetools.readthedocs.io/en/latest/>`_ library. Use this, if you want to use `arbitrary callback_data <https://github.com/python-telegram-bot/python-telegram-bot/wiki/Arbitrary-callback_data>`_.","+* ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[rate-limiter]\"`` installs `aiolimiter>=1.3,<1.4 <https://aiolimiter.readthedocs.io/en/stable/>`_. Use this, if you want to use ``telegram.ext.AIORateLimiter``.","+* ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[webhooks]\"`` installs the `tornado~=6.5 <https://www.tornadoweb.org/en/stable/>`_ library. Use this, if you want to use ``telegram.ext.Updater.start_webhook``/``telegram.ext.Application.run_webhook``.","+* ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[callback-data]\"`` installs the `cachetools>=8.0.0,<8.1.0 <https://cachetools.readthedocs.io/en/latest/>`_ library. Use this, if you want to use `arbitrary callback_data <https://github.com/python-telegram-bot/python-telegram-bot/wiki/Arbitrary-callback_data>`_."," * ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[job-queue]\"`` installs the `APScheduler>=3.10.4,<3.12.0 <https://apscheduler.readthedocs.io/en/3.x/>`_ library. Use this, if you want to use the ``telegram.ext.JobQueue``."," "," To install multiple optional dependencies, separate them by commas, e.g. ``pip install \"python-telegram-bot[socks,webhooks]\"``."],"additions":3,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"changes/config.py","lines":["@@ -34,6 +34,13 @@ class ChangoSectionChangeNote(","     OWNER =